    "durationMs": 237617,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built in /workspace:\n\n**Implementation** — ASP.NET Core 8 minimal APIs with EF Core 8 + Npgsql (the idiomatic persistence layer):\n- `Program.cs` — all endpoints, plus a `migrate` subcommand used by start.sh\n- `Link.cs` / `AppDbContext.cs` — entity and DbContext with a unique index on `Code`\n- `LinkApi.cs` — DTOs, code validation (4–20 ASCII letters/digits/`-`/`_`), and `DATABASE_URL` PostgreSQL-URL → Npgsql connection-string parsing (no hard-coded credentials)\n- `Migrations/` — EF Core migration creating the `Links` table with a unique code index\n\n**Verified behavior** (all via live HTTP tests):\n- POST /links: 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, submitted URL returned unchanged; generated 8-char codes; 409 on duplicate custom code; 422 for malformed JSON, missing/invalid url (non-absolute, non-http(s), no host), and invalid codes\n- GET /links/{code}: 200 or 404 JSON error; invalid code format → 422\n- GET /r/{code}: 302 with Location exactly the stored URL; clicks increment exactly once per request — confirmed under 30 parallel redirects (3 → 33)\n- GET /links: `{items, total}` in ascending creation order\n- Persistence: killed and restarted via start.sh — data and click counts survived; migrations are idempotent on re-run\n\n**Startup**: `sh start.sh` (executable, prebuilt Release binary) applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000. Dependencies were installed during the session, not in the script. README includes a \"Running the server\" section.\n\nI left the database clean and port 8000 free for the test suite."
  }
